// Firebase CLI config. Deliberately MINIMAL and firestore-only.
//
// This file exists because without it `firebase deploy --only firestore:rules`
// fails with "Not in a Firebase app directory (could not locate firebase.json)",
// which means the rules were NEVER deployable from this repo -- only editable by
// hand in the console, which is how the deployed copy and the repo drifted apart.
// See lessons-learned L37.
//
// Do NOT add sections for targets this project does not deploy (no hosting, no
// functions, no emulators). Declaring a target that is not really deployed is how
// a config starts lying about what exists. Add a section in the same commit that
// deploys it.
//
// The rationale for this note is a real `//` comment above, NOT a `"//"` KEY.
// A `"//"` key is not a comment to any parser that is not specifically
// forgiving, and firebase.json is read by more than one tool. It is the exact
// shape that has made other JSON/JSONC configs fail to load outright, and it is
// how a file that looks commented turns out to have an invalid key in it.
{
  "firestore": {
    "rules": "firestore/firestore.rules"
  }
}